  "description": "Widgets that fill the gaps .NET MAUI leaves: SmrBadgeView puts a count or a dot over any view, SmrTapBehavior runs a different command for one tap, a double tap, or five, SmrField puts a title and an error around an input, SmrEntry and four more inputs draw their box alike on every platform, as a line under the text or a border with rounded corners, and SmrDatePicker and SmrTimePicker take a date and a time that can each stay empty.",
